@* Imports a character from a file somebody picked — the other half of **"Download to keep"** on
   the review step.

   Not "Download as data", which was what this comment first said: that button writes the *report*,
   carrying derived stats, costs and every finding, and the strict reader refuses it — correctly,
   since reading it back would rebuild a character from its own conclusions. "Download to keep"
   exists because of this component: when it was written there was nothing in the app it could
   accept, which nobody had noticed because each half was right on its own.

   Self-contained: the picker, the read, and the message for whichever of the three ways a
   file can fail to become a character. Nothing here decides where a successful import
   goes — that is the hosting page's job, through OnImported — and nothing here can take
   the page down: CharacterImport never throws, so a bad file is an ordinary outcome shown
   right here rather than a page that stops rendering. *@

@inject CharacterImport Import

<Field Label="Import a character" For="import-character-file">
    <InputFile id="import-character-file" accept=".json,application/json"
               disabled="@_busy" OnChange="HandleSelected" />
</Field>

@if (_busy)
{
    <p class="small muted">Reading…</p>
}
else if (_message is not null)
{
    <p role="alert">@_message</p>
}

@code {
    // A character's own data is a few kilobytes even with every Power on the list bought.
    // This is headroom against a mistaken pick, not a target — the read fails politely
    // either way, so there is nothing to gain by being generous here.
    private const long MaxFileBytes = 2 * 1024 * 1024;

    private bool _busy;
    private string? _message;

    /// <summary>
    /// Raised once a file has become a character the rules can answer for. What happens to
    /// it — held, saved, replacing whatever is on screen — is the hosting page's decision,
    /// never this component's.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public EventCallback<(CharacterSheet Sheet, SheetMode Mode)> OnImported { get; set; }

    private async Task HandleSelected(InputFileChangeEventArgs e)
    {
        _busy = true;
        _message = null;

        try
        {
            string text;

            // The stream is read fully before the reader that could throw for an oversized
            // pick has a chance to leave a half-read file behind for the next attempt.
            await using (var stream = e.File.OpenReadStream(MaxFileBytes))
            using (var reader = new StreamReader(stream))
                text = await reader.ReadToEndAsync();

            var result = Import.Read(text);

            if (result.Imported is { } imported)
                await OnImported.InvokeAsync(imported);
            else
                _message = result.Message;
        }
        catch (IOException)
        {
            // OpenReadStream's own refusal for a pick over MaxFileBytes. Not a
            // CharacterImport outcome because there is no text yet to hand it.
            _message = "That file is too large to be a character exported from this app.";
        }
        finally
        {
            _busy = false;
        }
    }
}
